nodecode-crew is a rewrite of macd2's macd2/Crew:

  https://github.com/macd2/Crew
  commit ffb0e0c1d11a5fb3d36c3e34671bbd4c2cc02b6f
  Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE). The repository's LICENSE carries the standard
  Apache text with no copyright line filled in; its author, and the holder of
  this credit, is macd2.

cell.lisp rewrites, in Common Lisp, what the plugin's card, card script and
safety module do in Python (its __init__.py and scripts/crew_card.py,
scripts/crew_safety.py and scripts/crew_coordinator.py): a card is a plist in
one readable file under the home, opened only on a complete contract of goal,
artifact, done-when and proof command; the proof runs through a real shell,
bounded in the image, in the session's folder; every run is a line in the
card's verdict log and only a run that exits 0 passes the card; units of work
are marked with evidence; and the hardline floor (a root wipe, a mkfs, a
/dev write, a fork bomb) refuses a proof before it can run unattended. The five
tools keep the plugin's names and division: crew_plan, crew_verdict,
crew_progress, crew_diagnose, crew_proof_check.

Left out: the coordinator and verifier role profiles, the detached loop and the
twelve hooks that drove them, the Hermes kanban database, the per-card token
budget as a hard stop between turns (here the budget is a field, and a spent
one refuses the next proof), the systemd dashboard and the tailnet publish,
the Hermes Desktop surface and the transcript excerpts. Each of them is Hermes
plumbing rather than the thing a user asks for, and none of them survives a
move to a harness without Hermes profiles.
